  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1205 PM CDT Thu Jul 2 2026\n\nThe immediate forecast is of concern regarding convective\npotential. The 00Z and 12Z CAMs are all over the place. Surface\nand MLCAPE's are well into the mid thousands Joules already. \nWhile lacking upper support, downdraft CAPE suggests a \npotential damaging wind hazard from collapsing storms, if they \nmaterialize. And while the higher threat is to our southeast, \nwe'll have to watch closely if any can get going here in this \nhigh CAPE/low shear environ.\n\nDangerously high heat/humidity continues into the weekend. But \nwith a daily pop uptick that carries thru the weekend right on \ninto next week, at some point the convection and debris cloud \nmutes us off the headline numbers. It'll still be warm/humid, it\nis mid-summer after all; but the headline extremities should \neventually cease. Until then, we'll keep 'em going with high \nvisibility into the Semiquincentennial holiday weekend. As a \nresult, per collaboration, we extended the headline thru \nIndependence Day (Advisory), and will address any headline moves\nthereafter on a day-to-day basis.",
